00:04:01.787 --> 00:04:02.890
"What is the point?"

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.600
I'm gonna tell you this answer
in a very roundabout way.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.320
You'll probably be confused at first.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.150
When we're trying to create robots,

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.080
you may think that the
most difficult thing

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.400
for us to recreate in a robot

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.710
that is human like, is the eye.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.370
Wrong, we've done it so many times.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.730
The ear, wrong, we've
done it so many times.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.880
It's walking upright.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.230
Being able to navigate,

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:26.100
steps, slipping, heels,
angles, pushes, force.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.710
All of that takes an enormous
amount of coordination.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.580
Constant firing of neurons.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.290
Flexing and relaxing and
extension of muscles.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.600
When that happens, it's very
easy for a muscle to fire

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.340
either in the wrong pattern
or get thrown off balance,

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.990
and therefore creating a micro tear.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.310
When a micro tear is
formed inside a muscle,

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:45.500
the muscle actually
spasms to protect itself.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:49.000
The reason why massaging feels
good, why icing feels good,

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.070
because it actually allows

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.830
the muscle to get more
circulation and heal itself.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.770
So it's not like the body
is causing it self-damage,

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.990
it's more like the outside world

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.520
causes all sorts of scary situations

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.420
that your body deals with very well.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.770
That instead of dying,
you get a muscle spasm.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.340
I think it's a worthy trade off.

